<title>USA: Innkeepers USA Trust Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Innkeepers USA Trust Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>PALM BEACH, Fla. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended</p>
<p>						   3/31/97	  3/31/96</p>
<p> Total revenue				   12,725	    5,790</p>
<p> Net income					4,230	    2,115</p>
<p> Net income per common share		  0.19	     0.20</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>of common shares and</p>
<p>common share equivalents</p>
<p>  outstanding			     23,583,810     11,568,591</p>
<p> Funds from operations			  8,798	   3,717</p>
<p> Funds from operations per share	     0.32	    0.32</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>and common share</p>
<p>  equivalents outstanding		    27,647	  11,569</p>
<p>		(in thousands, except share and per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  The weighted average common shares outstanding in the first quarter of 1997, FFO per share was impacted by the more than doubled number of common shares outstanding compared to the prior year quarter, which was due to the company's second follow-on offering in October of 1996.  Proceeds from the offering were used for the acquisition of ten hotels, which have historically yielded the strongest results in the second and third quarters.</p>
</text>
